wine (11.18~git2.df15af3-3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Add patch 622 (ntdll/virtual): KakaoTalk's Themida-style protector
    passes garbage page protections (e.g. 0x6dbb15d2) to
    NtProtectVirtualMemory when its obfuscated operand decoding
    mis-decodes under FEX emulation, and retries forever on
    STATUS_INVALID_PAGE_PROTECTION. Normalize unknown protection
    values to PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE for image pages so the
    unpacker can proceed. (The client still parks itself at a later
    protector gate; the FEX-side mis-decode remains open upstream.)

 -- yjlee <yjlee@localhost>  Fri, 26 Sep 2026 04:00:00 +0900

wine (11.18~git2.df15af3-2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Fix 32-bit (WoW64/FEX) process startup: dpkg hardening flags added
    -mbranch-protection=standard to the unix-side build, which breaks
    wine on armv8.6-a (Apple Silicon) per the Fedora spec; strip it via
    DEB_CFLAGS_MAINT_STRIP / DEB_CXXFLAGS_MAINT_STRIP.
  * Add patch 621 (mscoree): never block boot on the wine-mono MSI
    bootstrap. The wine-mono installer custom action targets a
    different architecture than ARM64EC msiexec, and dl.winehq.org no
    longer serves the generic wine-mono-11.3.0.msi.
  * Ship the wine-mono 11.3.0 (arm64) runtime tree in wine-core at
    /usr/share/wine/mono/wine-mono-11.3.0; mscoree finds it via
    get_mono_path_unix, so .NET apps work without any MSI install.

 -- yjlee <yjlee@localhost>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 04:10:00 +0900

